 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T17:06:13.241033Z",
 "text": "The clause is enforceable. Section 107 of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* requires a landlord to pay interest on a rent deposit each year at the rate set by the rent increase guideline. The clause tracks that obligation: the rate is the guideline, and it is applied when each annual payment falls due. Because the clause matches the statutory rule, it does not conflict with the Act's non-waiver provision in section 4, which voids terms that give a tenant less than the Act provides.\n\nSection 107 has its own mechanics, including the timing of payments and how interest is calculated. Those details could affect how a particular payment is computed, but they do not make this clause unenforceable.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 107",
